---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — DearSQL"
  description="DearSQL privacy policy. We collect minimal data and never sell it."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy Policy", url: "/privacy" },
  ]}
>
  <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-6 text-sm">
    <h1 class="text-xl font-bold mb-1 before:content-['##_']">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-subtext0 text-xs mb-6">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-subtext0">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-bold text-text mb-2 before:content-['###_']">What we collect</h2>
        <p>DearSQL collects minimal data:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 ml-2">
          <li>
            - <span class="text-text">Bug reports</span> — submitted voluntarily via
            the "report bug" form. Filed as GitHub issues. Includes your description
            and any screenshots you attach.
          </li>
          <li>
            - <span class="text-text">License validation</span> — when you activate
            a Pro license, your license key and a device identifier are sent to Polar.sh
            to verify the activation. We do not store this on our own servers.
          </li>
          <li>
            - <span class="text-text">Purchase data</span> — handled entirely by Polar.sh.
            We receive your email address when you buy a license. We do not store
            payment details.
          </li>
          <li>
            - <span class="text-text">Crash reports</span> — the desktop app uses
            <a href="https://sentry.io" target="_blank">Sentry</a>. If the app crashes, a
            crash report is sent: the stack trace, a memory dump of the crashed process,
            app version and OS, and a short trail of recent app events (theme or workspace
            changes, and the text of recent query error messages, which can quote values
            from your data). Each launch also sends an anonymous session record (start,
            end, whether it crashed) used to measure crash rates. No queries, results or
            credentials are sent otherwise.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-bold text-text mb-2 before:content-['###_']">What we don't collect</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 ml-2">
          <li>- No analytics or tracking on this website, except a Google Ads conversion event on the purchase confirmation page (used only to measure completed purchases)</li>
          <li>- No usage analytics from the desktop app: crash reports only (above)</li>
          <li>- No access to your database credentials, and no query data except what a crash report may contain (above)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-bold text-text mb-2 before:content-['###_']">Third-party services</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 ml-2">
          <li>
            - <a href="https://polar.sh" target="_blank">Polar.sh</a> — payment and
            license management
          </li>
          <li>
            - <a href="https://ads.google.com" target="_blank">Google Ads</a> — conversion
            tracking on the checkout confirmation page only
          </li>
          <li>
            - <a href="https://sentry.io" target="_blank">Sentry</a> — crash reports from
            the desktop app
          </li>
          <li>
            - AI providers you choose (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, or a coding agent such as
            Claude Code or Codex) — only when you use the AI features, and they receive the
            messages, schema and query results you send them. DearSQL does not see this data.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Each service has its own privacy policy governing data they collect.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
